[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Vue Router: Guards, Lazy Loading, and Dynamic Routes in Vue.js"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Modern single-page applications built with Vue.js require sophisticated routing strategies to maintain high performance and secure access to specific views. This tutorial explores advanced Vue Router concepts including navigation guards, lazy loading, and dynamic routes."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Dynamic Routes"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Dynamic routes allow you to map a given pattern to the same component. This is essential for handling resources like user profiles or product details where the URL segment changes based on data IDs."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"const routes = [
  {
    path: '/user/:id',
    name: 'UserProfile',
    component: UserProfile,
    props: true
  }
];"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"By setting "props: true", the route parameter "id" is automatically passed down to the UserProfile component as a prop, decoupling the component from the router instance."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Lazy Loading Routes"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"When building large applications, downloading the entire JavaScript bundle on initial load degrades performance. Lazy loading defers loading route components until the user actually navigates to that specific route using dynamic imports."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"const routes = [
  {
    path: '/dashboard',
    name: 'Dashboard',
    component: () => import('./views/Dashboard.vue')
  }
];"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Navigation Guards"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"Navigation guards are used to protect routes by redirecting users or canceling navigation based on authentication states or permissions. Vue Router provides global, per-route, and in-component guards."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"const router = createRouter({ ... });

router.beforeEach((to, from, next) => {
  const isAuthenticated = localStorage.getItem('token');
  if (to.meta.requiresAuth && !isAuthenticated) {
    next({ name: 'Login' });
  } else {
    next();
  }
});"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Summary of Best Practices"},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always enable route props when utilizing dynamic routes to keep components modular and testable."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Implement lazy loading for all non-critical paths to significantly reduce initial application load times."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use route metadata ("meta") properties inside your router configuration to cleanly define security requirements for global navigation guards."}]
